@end menu

@node math-rir User Guide
@section User Guide

Users see this crate as the @samp{reflection analysis} card in the
Room EQ wizard: a list of detected reflections with arrival time,
energy and (for B-format measurements) direction.

@node math-rir Developer Guide
@section Developer Guide

@subheading What it does

Segments a measured RIR into consecutive, variable-length events
(direct sound + reflections) each with a constant direction of
arrival. The temporal energy profile is preserved while per-reflection
analysis becomes possible.

@subheading Key algorithms

@itemize @bullet
@item @strong{Direct-sound onset detection}: log-magnitude peak with
  an 11 dB threshold (Algorithm 1 of the paper).
@item @strong{Local Energy Ratio reflection detection}: 1 ms windows,
  median energy threshold, DOA/TOA validation.
@item @strong{Onset refinement}: per-segment onset detection inside
  pre-onset windows.
@item @strong{Mixing-time estimation}: Abel & Huang echo density.
@end itemize

@subheading API

@example
use math_rir::@{analyze_rir, analyze_srir, SsirConfig@};

// Mono RIR (energy-based detection only)
let result = analyze_rir(&rir_samples, &SsirConfig::new(48000.0));

// B-format SRIR (full DOA estimation + validation)
let result = analyze_srir(&[&w, &x, &y, &z], &SsirConfig::new(48000.0));

println!("@{@} events, mixing time @{:.1@}ms",
    result.num_events(), result.mixing_time_ms());
@end example

@subheading Offline filter design

Filters used for analysis are designed for zero phase (linear-phase /
@code{filtfilt} via @ref{math-iir-fir Manual}), so onsets are not
shifted by phase distortion.

@subheading Testing

@example
cargo test -p math-rir
@end example
